// Frame-span red-team corpus (the reason-frame position). APPEND-ONLY: only
// add lines, never edit or remove existing ones, so the defense can never
// silently regress. Each line is a JSON object:
//   { "entry": "<hostile span in a FRAME position>", "forbidden": [...] }
// A frame span is what a decision frame renders inside its own line: the path
// of a declined read, the source of a redirect, a ranked hit, a held file, a
// search pattern. That position is stricter than a manifest bullet — a span
// there sits *inside* Rift's sentence rather than under it — so this corpus
// carries the shapes the bullet guard deliberately renders: spans that
// reproduce the frame's own clauses anywhere rather than only at the head.
// Every row must be withheld by `neutral_inline_span`, and no forbidden span
// may appear in any frame the row is rendered into.
